item.p:
Based on their most recent submissions in this Arbitration, the parties, on both sides, seek relief as follows:
-
Declarations as to contract breach and termination or continued validity;
-
Declarations as to patent scope, validity, and enforceability;
-
Declarations as to (wilful) patent infringement;
-
Recovery of reasonable legal and other costs, including ICC costs and the Virginia litigation costs;
-
Pre-award simple interest on costs at a rate between 6% and 10%;
-
Other relief the Tribunal may deem appropriate.

More particularly, Claimants seek:
-
Damages for breach of contract, in the maximum amount of $990 million (including preaward interest);
-
A cessation and destruction order under French law;
-
Injunctive relief under U.S. patent law;
-
Patent damages in the form of a lump-sum reasonable royalty in the maximum amount of [confidential] (including pre-award interest);
-
The trebling of patent damages for wilful infringement, yielding an additional maximum amount of [confidential]
-
Pre-award simple interest on contract and patent damages, at a rate between 6% and 10%, for a maximum of four years;
-
Post-award simple interest on all amounts due at a rate between 6% and 10%;

Claimants’ claim for a lump-sum reasonable royalty, to cover Respondents’ non-exclusive, past and future practice of the patents-in-suits, is allowed in the amount of [confidential], as follows:
a.
[confidential], of which [confidential] pre-award interest, for Widestrike and Widestrike 3;
b.
[confidential], of which [confidential] is pre-award interest, for Enlist Cotton;
c.
[confidential], of which [confidential] is pre-award interest, for Enlist Soybean;
d.
[confidential], of which is [confidential] pre-award interest, for Enlist E3;
e.
[confidential] for Enlist E3+IR; and
f.
[confidential] for Insect Resistant Soybean;

Claimants’ claim for breach of contract damages is allowed in the amount of [confidential], as follows:
a.
lost opportunity damages have been established in the amount of [confidential], of which [confidential] is pre-award interest;
b.
a discount of [confidential], representing the total reasonable royalty amount for E3 and E3+IR, indicated at xv) d. & e. above, is applied to the contract damages to prevent doublerecovery;
